    "version" : "2.2.0",
    "author" : [ "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0438-6831" ],
    "description" : {
      "undefined" : "The Spatiotemporal module is part of the LCAnet ontology proposed by the SmartACV Carnot Project.\n            It provides a formal representation of spatial and temporal aspects relevant to the LCA process,\n            enabling the modeling and integration of location- and time-specific data for products or services.\n            For the temporal aspect, it reuses classes and properties by importing the Time ontology: Time instant,\n            Time interval, and DurationDescription. For the spatial aspect, it aligns with some pre-defined classes \n            from other ontologies such as the Feature class from the geonames vocabulary."
    },
    "labels" : {
      "undefined" : "LCAnet-Spatiotemporal"
    },
